     "t": "p",
     "x": "Honestly Pookie, this has been so hard. I don't even know where to begin. We've been working for over 36 hours genuinely nonstop 4 AM in the night. I've never been so cold sore and alone. I saw a kid try to kill himself in front of me before he got tackled I even hate my retarded bunk mate. After 40 hours we lined up outside for 40 minutes to sleep now Drill Sergeant told us some PT's and 3 AM day start. It's 11 PM now so cold and so much blood taken I imagine all day what I get to write to you but now that I have a moment, I just wanna cry, but I have to do another hours. I'm not gonna quit. I know I can't. It's worth it but genuinely every second here is pain I cannot believe how much I took for granted I'm so exhausted. I wish I could sleep in the 20 degree nights. I've been nearly fainting every few minutes generally, my eyes close my body falls forward. IDK. I also hate a lot of people here, which is unlike me and I'm good.",
