    {
     "t": "p",
     "x": "Day three I finally have some time to journal tonight. I had firewatch so I have to stay up until 2230 which is 10:30 PM which is not bad. Anyways the bars are cramped to squeaky and full of extremely immature people. I don't mean all or even most but enough they talk and yell all night keeping everyone awake and intro they cannot shut the fuck up and we keep getting punished Those bunch or just jar head enough to think it's all a game my day consist of wake at 4 AM be outside by 4:30 shiver stay silent for three hours. It's just so tough. I hear reception is the hard part and it's supposed to be up from here. I'm feeling kind of better like I accepted. Life will be bad for three months but now I'm writing it down. I miss you so fucking much. It's crazy every day not knowing I can get my phone. It's so hard I want even a minute"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "x": "I feel like I should summarize we arrive here we went to the classroom got boots waited outside to get Camelback and PT. This takes seven hours in the cold sleep 20 minutes. We read three hours in an auditorium eating meals outside in the cold so much blood work optometry CAC card Tons of forms so I can't try to kill himself.",
     "c": "I feel like I should summarize we arrive here we went to the classroom got boots waited outside to get CamelBak and PT. This takes seven hours in the cold sleep 20 minutes. We read three hours in an auditorium eating meals outside in the cold so much blood work optometry CAC card Tons of forms so I can't try to kill himself."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "x": "Honestly I hate to hear nothing good I wish I could hear your thoughts on you. I don't want to return a failure. A big part of me almost hoped I could get blood results back and I have disease like cancer or something like that that dismisses me so that way I don't quit or fail. They had a moment for people to admit without trouble. A few people did I could've said something like I did drugs in the past, but I stayed silent so I stayed there's a few people I'm friendly with, but so many here are just so immature I like being goofy, but this is so cringe. I feel like a black sheep, not that it matters, but it's so strange to think these people see me as a quiet kid, but I'm 25. Everyone thinks I'm just young. I just feel extra distant. I try to talk to staff Sarge to get my phone but failed. I'm gonna try again"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "x": "When I'm home. I only wanna nap for 24 hours. I don't wanna do this again. I've not felt happy or smiled or accomplished anything since I've been here genuinely I have not overheard a joke a funny event nothing I wish I did summer because my body's permanently it's stiff from shivers. My mouth is bleeding for my teeth, chattering I thought all day of things I want to share, but there's no way to romanticize the hollow emptiness this place brings."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "x": "I find out tomorrow when I'm shipped either Friday or Tuesday each day impacts when I'm out so I might be longer thank God. This is national guard. I cannot imagine the full years if it was full army failure is not an option. I know stories of people breaking their bones and they get stuck here. It's not that deep I still feel so stiff. This feels like a party. You don't want to go to, but you have to only this time I cannot exit. I've learned my life lessons. I just wanna go home literally more than anything. I don't even have privacy to journal or cry. I'm not a fuck up either. I'm actually doing really well With every task they give me. I just hate it. 16 hours of standing silent and freezing winters broken up by getting punished by some dip shit mistake. I just need us to be over. I need reception and I'd rather do that gas tank room every day than this."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "x": "I'm gonna find a way to call you. I have firewatch soon. I wanted to talk more about the memories. I'm thinking of to stay sane, but everyone saying one day feels like five days. I literally love you so much. I give up Legos Fortnite movies fucking anything to have you again This literally hurts my body how much I need you. I always knew I was lucky and that I would miss you, but it's like a weight in my chest. That's dragging me down into the bottom of the ocean. Your love was so out of this world. It seemed almost unreal now like that life was a dream because everything is so different now I think I belong with you not here I used to be excited about The money I can make on a deployment now I kinda don't want it at all. I wish I didn't have to do this. You deserve a happy life and be able to buy anything you ever wanted. I'm sorry that isn't me. I wish I had more to give you so I did not have to be here."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "x": "I was wrong about everything there's no time to write to eat to bond no time to talk to think to sleep. I thought it would just be 14 hour workouts with an hour to call every week and then some shit talking but this is not that it's so much more. I literally don't even know how to be happy here. I cannot be thinking of the things I miss. I wish I could write better like I wanted, but maybe I won't even send these. I don't know if I'm too gullible, naive, optimistic, retarded, prideful or something else I would go back in time to tell myself not to leave. Do not join spend as much time with Sarah as you can."
    }
