     "c": "we got into the formation had a quick safety brief Hubbard accidentally tried Sitting with the girls, which was funny then first platoon lined up to shoot. It took them 2 1/2 hours to group and zero their shots second platoon was freezing by 12:45. We finally got to shoot. I built the house. I loaded makeready weapons free. My groupings were so good drill sergeant when he checked the targets After Every five told me to show the battalion commander who is a former Green Beret he chose to hold onto it to show him later, so I felt pretty cool. I might be best in the platoon. We cross the street after clearing our weapons had MRE for the first time. I finally stopped shivering and for the first time we are allowed to quietly talk with each other."
