     "t": "p",
     "x": "I've not seen my brother in 12 Years my grandparents passed around them too. My mother lost her three years ago all those homes I was thinking about I've not seen in like 20 years. My dad left for most of my life via divorce on 25 now in the army the memories feel so important. I think it's what I'll see if my life flashes before me. It feels important. It actually feels like the most important things I have feels like all I have. I miss how it all felt the love the wonder the warmth everything was worthy of curiosity I could love things without baggage even toys or shows. They all seem to be full of heart now I'm just too analytical and artsy feel like I cannot feel all anymore or excitement. These grand encompassing lenses. I wish that everything could feel is real forever. If anything could be this good again maybe I just need to write my book and God forbid if I ran takes me I won't have any regrets because I'll have left that book behind and if it does take me at least I could see my mother in the dearly departed."
