     "t": "p",
     "x": "My reflections last night helped me articulate my sins during confession. I was nervous yet calm, almost as if I tried to be nervous about it, but in a room of open arms, there was never fear or anxiety to be had, I was in every sense of the term blessed to have the priest that I did. I had an in these confessions our routine and I would just be hand, waved away and told to say a few Hail Mary is nothing more, but he listened he felt he reflected he was that Menter I craved so bad. My voice remain a steady of steel yet my eyes poured like a faucet onto the bleacher chairs. I told him how good I was at lying to myself to justify stealing lust, jealousy, alcohol, drugs, and how bad I can be counting my blessings and how I was even angry. God took my mother so soon I was reminded I could still live for her, even though I won't be able to count every blessing there's always blessings to be count The hairs on my head the senses even all kinds of blessings. I was thankful to be in a place that challenges me although he phrased it much better basically I felt relieved a huge weight off my shoulders and made me happy to worship and shake everyone's hand.",
