     "x": "I thought about studying for land navigation I thought about Venice in Dutch Republic sea faring democratic financial systems I thought about how monopolized asteroid mining could be for my sci-fi book I thought about a lot of things. This will only make sense to me, but I thought about maybe some religious groups can censor entertainment and that's why entertainment is not a big media in the sci-fi world because everything has to get through the religious censorship. I thought about in the sci-fi war maybe there was hack water treatment or maybe like someone poisoned water space clouds I thought about how instead of hyper space like instead of just teleporting, it's kind of like instead of walking towards a tennis ball for example, you bring a tennis ball to you like you changed both locations I thought about maybe planets could be alive in their core is this energy that is nearly infinite fuel I thought about a planner that looks like an underwater coral reef, but with no water And it's very vibrant because the life that evolved there has a different wavelength I thought about anti-ship laser devices I thought about in the book maybe planets are very small. I thought about the character Quinn wiping his face ID I thought about a planet that can mirror light but magnify it so it could be a dull red sun at daytime but could have an intense nighttime where it's actually brighter I thought about the religions about how they could have the origin of man and creation myths I want to study other planet tectonic plates I thought about religious rituals involving minerals. I thought about vaccines as a plot patch. I thought about holidays"
