   "title": "The polygraph detail",
   "ch": "last",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "p",
     "x": "Today must've been the hottest day in all of basic. I volunteered yesterday to go on detail today. I was told it would be freezing and we could wear waffles so after PT we started marching at what I thought would be scrubbing and cleaning all day we went across the street for national center of credibility assessment and we were greeted with the wall of logos like FBICIA ATFOCS and everything we were told to participate in a polygraph test we were there to train new examiners and we'd stay in the warmth of a comfy chairs. We got to watch movies. We saw a major pain. Bruce Almighty end of watch ends ended it with the amazing Spider-Man"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "x": "but if you noticed that's a lot of movies and not a lot of testing that's because they never pick for my paper from the pile, it may sound silly, but I was a bit sad and truth is it's been a while That I was in a room where I truly felt like I belonged not in terms of love, but life roles, it felt appropriate to be in that building with a blended prestige intelligence without having pretentious or being unapproachable. I like knowing that they're is capable people around me so many jobs or places I don't have that rigorous ambition after getting my degree in psychology I finally felt that this was meaningful but I don't know. Maybe I dodged a bullet or something."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "x": "Also I'm still mad about not having a rank so on my army dress blues no mail but today was like this. It was really good and then pretty boring. We ran 3 miles for PT. I struggled more than usual. I chilled with Libby, Arthur, Maxine Merritt and lemon I'm gonna shower some songs I thought of our plush by the Stone Temple Pilots shattered and a bloody Sunday by U2. Oh happy St. Patrick's Day reflecting on how different this day would be if I was home I hope the Halsey and Reagan hyped up about reading the Bible."
    }
   ],
